# x16emu -mousescript (gate N): a release the program never sees.
# Klondike #1, the test build with SOL_SLOWTICK (the second's process holds
# the main loop for 12 frames, sol_slow 1 meanwhile; SLOW is its address,
# from the map). The talon clicked (a move: the clock runs); the ace of
# hearts (row 5) pressed and dragged a little; during the slow pass the
# button goes up and down again: the kernel reports one press, the release
# is lost. Then a move down and the release. The drag must not leave its
# outline on the table (the hardware report: a line through a foundation).
# The drag starts after a slow pass has ended (the second's process runs
# at its own phase: a talon click that takes longer, Veranda Look 2's felt,
# moved it; the press and release of the talon may both fall in the first
# pass), and the release and press come in the next one.
0 id 3
400 move -2000 -2000
440 move 76 33
442 down
446 up
wait SLOW 1
wait SLOW 0
5 move 400 136
7 down
10 move 3 2
wait SLOW 1
1 up
3 down
40 move 0 30
50 move 0 30
60 move 0 30
70 up
400 exit
